Ported code
-----------
crates/neighbors (milestone M9) is a Rust port of:

- Annoy 1.17.3, as bundled in RcppAnnoy 0.0.23 (inst/include/annoylib.h and
  kissrandom.h): Copyright (c) 2013 Spotify AB, licensed under the Apache
  License, Version 2.0 (third_party/licenses/Apache-2.0.txt). Changes: the
  index build (two_means, create_split, side, _make_tree, _split_imbalance),
  the search (_get_all_nns), the node layout and file format, and the
  Kiss64Random generator, for the Euclidean, Angular and Manhattan metrics,
  translated statement by statement into Rust (crates/neighbors/src/annoy.rs
  and kiss.rs); the multi-threaded build, on-disk build, mmap loading, the
  DotProduct and Hamming metrics and the other generators are not ported.
  Annoy's principal author is Erik Bernhardsson.
- RcppAnnoy 0.0.23 (Dirk Eddelbuettel, GPL (>= 2)): its conversions of R's
  doubles to the index's floats (addItem, getNNsByVectorList).
- Seurat 5.5.1 (Copyright 2021 Seurat authors, MIT): FindNeighbors' Annoy
  path (AnnoyBuildIndex, AnnoySearch, the k adjustment) and ComputeSNN
  (src/snn.cpp), in crates/neighbors/src/lib.rs and graph.rs.
- The GNU C++ library (libstdc++, GCC; GPL-3 with the GCC Runtime Library
  Exception): std::priority_queue's push_heap and pop_heap and
  std::partial_sort (bits/stl_heap.h, bits/stl_algo.h), whose exact moves
  Annoy's search depends on, in crates/neighbors/src/stl.rs.

crates/cluster (milestone M10) is a Rust port of:

- Seurat 5.5.1 (Copyright 2021 Seurat authors, MIT): src/ModularityOptimizer.cpp
  and src/RModularityOptimizer.cpp, Seurat's C++ translation of Ludo Waltman
  and Nees Jan van Eck's ModularityOptimizer 1.3.0 (the Java program of
  http://www.ludowaltman.nl/slm/, which implements their smart local moving
  algorithm and the Louvain algorithm of Blondel et al.). Changes: the
  JavaRandom generator (java.util.Random's nextInt, with its power-of-two
  branch and its 32-bit wrap-around) and generateRandomPermutation, the
  Clustering and Network classes (matrixToNetwork, createReducedNetwork,
  createSubnetworks), VOSClusteringTechnique's calcQualityFunction, local
  moving, Louvain, Louvain with multilevel refinement and smart local moving,
  and RunModularityClusteringCpp's random starts, best start, printed output
  and orderClustersByNNodes, translated statement by statement into Rust
  (crates/cluster/src/java_random.rs, clustering.rs, network.rs, vos.rs,
  optimizer.rs); the standalone main(), the edge-file reader,
  identifyComponents, removeCluster and removeSmallClusters, which
  FindClusters does not use, are not ported. The network and clustering are
  passed by reference instead of shared_ptr; the arithmetic and every order
  of operations are the C++'s.
- Seurat 5.5.1's R code (MIT): GroupSingletons, FindClusters.default's loop
  over the resolutions and FindClusters.Seurat's columns, level order and
  seurat_clusters (R/clustering.R), in crates/cluster/src/singletons.rs and
  find_clusters.rs. GroupSingletons' tie-breaking draw uses R's set.seed and
  sample, and its connectivity R's mean, from crates/rcompat (R, GPL (>= 2)).

